# Notebook voice

When drafting or editing matching files, follow `.cursor/skills/kiruk-notebook-voice/SKILL.md`.

- Spoken, feeling-first. Keep his slang. No TED/LinkedIn manifesto lines.
- Fix the *story* he means before polishing words.
- Marks: `<Mark>` phrase, `<Zig>` metaphor, `<Hit>` sentence, `<Note>` aside, `>` for other voices. Few per section.
- After a tone rejection, append `.cursor/skills/kiruk-notebook-voice/mistakes.md`.
